<item><title><![CDATA[Have you heard of the Library of Alexandria?]]></title><description><![CDATA[This guest post is for you if you've ever thought how things could be if we were more interested in pursuing knowledge instead of money.]]></description><link>https://dailypushes.substack.com/p/have-you-heard-of-the-library-of</link><guid isPermaLink="false">https://dailypushes.substack.com/p/have-you-heard-of-the-library-of</guid><dc:creator><![CDATA[Becario]]></dc:creator><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 05:21:25 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Z225!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5a30119c-4409-4b4d-b3da-f83360e8e445_1072x1090.jpeg" length="0" type="image/jpeg"/><content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><em>This post is written in Spanish on purpose. You don&#8217;t need to understand every word; just keep reading.</em></p><p>En el cap&#237;tulo de hoy de comprensi&#243;n lectora (o secci&#243;n &#8220;&#161;&#161;&#161;&#191;Pero qu&#233;?!!!&#8221; para los amigos), hablaremos de la Biblioteca de Alejandr&#237;a, una de tantas maravillas perdidas de la antiguedad.</p><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img" target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Z225!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5a30119c-4409-4b4d-b3da-f83360e8e445_1072x1090.jpeg" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div class="image2-inset"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Z225!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5a30119c-4409-4b4d-b3da-f83360e8e445_1072x1090.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Z225!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5a30119c-4409-4b4d-b3da-f83360e8e445_1072x1090.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Z225!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5a30119c-4409-4b4d-b3da-f83360e8e445_1072x1090.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Z225!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5a30119c-4409-4b4d-b3da-f83360e8e445_1072x1090.jpeg 1456w" sizes="100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Z225!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5a30119c-4409-4b4d-b3da-f83360e8e445_1072x1090.jpeg" width="1072" height="1090" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/5a30119c-4409-4b4d-b3da-f83360e8e445_1072x1090.jpeg&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:1090,&quot;width&quot;:1072,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:891106,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:true,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://dailypushes.substack.com/i/214755764?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5a30119c-4409-4b4d-b3da-f83360e8e445_1072x1090.jpeg&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" class="sizing-normal" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Z225!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5a30119c-4409-4b4d-b3da-f83360e8e445_1072x1090.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Z225!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5a30119c-4409-4b4d-b3da-f83360e8e445_1072x1090.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Z225!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5a30119c-4409-4b4d-b3da-f83360e8e445_1072x1090.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Z225!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5a30119c-4409-4b4d-b3da-f83360e8e445_1072x1090.jpeg 1456w" sizes="100vw" fetchpriority="high"></picture><div class="image-link-expand"><div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset"><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="var(--color-fg-primary)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon-noB79L"><g><path d="M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L"><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"></polyline><polyline points="9 21 3 21 3 15"></polyline><line x1="21" x2="14" y1="3" y2="10"></line><line x1="3" x2="10" y1="21" y2="14"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class="image-caption"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Library_of_Alexandria#cite_note-FOOTNOTEGarland200861-1">Nineteenth-century artistic rendering of the Library of Alexandria by the German artist O. Von Corven, based on the archaeological evidence available at that time</a></figcaption></figure></div><p class="button-wrapper" data-attrs="{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://dailypushes.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe now&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}" data-component-name="ButtonCreateButton"><a class="button primary" href="https://dailypushes.substack.com/subscribe?"><span>Subscribe now</span></a></p><div class="callout-block" data-callout="true"><p>Hace m&#225;s de dos mil a&#241;os, en la ciudad de Alejandr&#237;a, en Egipto, existi&#243; una de las bibliotecas m&#225;s importantes del mundo antiguo. La construy&#243; la dinast&#237;a ptolemaica en el siglo III a. C. y lleg&#243; a tener entre 400.000 y 700.000 libros antiguos en rollos de papel pergamino.</p><p></p><p>Esta biblioteca era parte de un gran centro para reunir y estudiar el saber de muchas culturas. Los estudiantes y cient&#237;ficos pod&#237;an encontrar all&#237; libros de matem&#225;ticas, astronom&#237;a, medicina, literatura, filosof&#237;a y geograf&#237;a.</p><p></p><p>Alejandr&#237;a estaba en un lugar excelente. Ten&#237;a un puerto internacional muy importante donde viajaban personas de muchos pa&#237;ses. Los gobernantes de la ciudad quer&#237;an que Alejandr&#237;a fuera el centro de la cultura y de las ideas. Por eso, intentaron conseguir una colecci&#243;n de textos muy grande.</p><p></p><p>En esa &#233;poca, los libros no eran como los de ahora; eran rollos de papel antiguo. Los directores de la biblioteca buscaban libros nuevos todo el tiempo. Se dice que cuando un barco llegaba al puerto, los guardias buscaban libros para copiarlos y guardarlos en la biblioteca.</p><p></p><p>Lo m&#225;s especial de este lugar no era solo el n&#250;mero de libros. Lo importante era la gran idea de reunir el conocimiento de diferentes pueblos en un mismo sitio para estudiarlo con l&#243;gica y calma.</p><p></p><p>La antigua biblioteca de Alejandr&#237;a es uno de los mayores &#233;xitos de la historia humana. Demuestra que era una sociedad que amaba aprender y que pensaba que comprender el mundo era algo muy importante.</p><p></p><p>Por desgracia, la mayor parte de esos libros se perdi&#243; para siempre debido a los incendios, la intolerancia religiosa, las guerras y la mala suerte. Cuando una sociedad pierde sus libros, no solo pierde objetos, sino tambi&#233;n muchos a&#241;os de descubrimientos.</p></div><h2>Cuestionario de autoevaluaci&#243;n:</h2><p>Veamos qu&#233; tal se te ha dado. No pasa nada si no has entendido todo a la primera. Intenta contestar todas las preguntas, y vuelve a repasar el texto si te falta alguna respuesta. &#161;Mucho &#225;nimo!</p><p>Suscr&#237;bete gratuitamente para ver el cuestionario. Y si te parece que el contenido lo vale, merece la pena, y te lo puedes permitir, tambi&#233;n puedes convertirte en suscriptor de pago para ayudar a que sigamos creando m&#225;s contenido como este.</p><p class="button-wrapper" data-attrs="{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://dailypushes.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe now&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}" data-component-name="ButtonCreateButton"><a class="button primary" href="https://dailypushes.substack.com/subscribe?"><span>Subscribe now</span></a></p><p>El cuestionario contiene preguntas de tipo test para evaluar tu comprensi&#243;n lectora.</p><p class="button-wrapper" data-attrs="{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://dailypushes.substack.com/p/have-you-heard-of-the-library-of?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Share&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:&quot;button-wrapper&quot;}" data-component-name="ButtonCreateButton"><a class="button primary button-wrapper" href="https://dailypushes.substack.com/p/have-you-heard-of-the-library-of?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share"><span>Share</span></a></p><p>Si te ha parecido interesante suscr&#237;bete, comparte, deja tus comentarios, o dale a &#8220;Like &#10084;&#65039;&#8221;. Eso nos ayuda a crecer y a seguir motivados, y te lo agradeceremos de coraz&#243;n.</p><p class="button-wrapper" data-attrs="{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://dailypushes.substack.com/p/have-you-heard-of-the-library-of/comments&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Leave a comment&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}" data-component-name="ButtonCreateButton"><a class="button primary" href="https://dailypushes.substack.com/p/have-you-heard-of-the-library-of/comments"><span>Leave a comment</span></a></p><p><strong>&#191;Y t&#250;? &#191;Conoc&#237;as la Biblioteca de Alejandr&#237;a?</strong></p>]]></content:encoded></item>